      "sourceTextSha256": "99eda58f7b1bb175b454f776400a1326f6b760d63fd323bafc7d88998af542b4",
      "text": "Breakfast, then a private tour (7 hours) with an English-speaking guide to the traditional town of Filandia: a walk through its colonial streets, the Quindío viewpoint (closed on Mondays, or Tuesdays after a Monday holiday) and a tasting experience with drinks and desserts at a local restaurant. Continue to the Cocora Valley: a welcome canelazo, an introduction to the reserve by a specialised eco-guide, a walk into the cloud forest and the wax palm, the world’s tallest palm and Colombia’s national tree, with the traditional Quindío wax palm ritual and the planting of palm seedlings. End in Salento with a walk through its colonial streets. Typical lunch included.",
